    "Notes Updated": "5/12/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "Pena should be getting way more love\n His raw power has jumped tremendously so far. He's gone from a 90th Percentile EV under 100 in the DSL to 106.5 early in the Low A season\n Hit tool looks like it could be plus still\n Swing decisions have improved greatly from the DSL, not nearly as much of a free swinger now\n Power in games is mostly doubles and triples right now, mainly because he needs to elevate his hard hit more often\n Glove has looked inconsistent, and I do have some concerns about the way he attacks the ball, I would like to see him in person when he gets to High A\n Speed is plus, though he's not a super smooth looking runner, only concerns me in whether it could cause injuries\n This is a top 50 prospect in baseball in my eyes, if not closer to top 20-30",
    "Notes Updated 2": "6/9/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Solid bat to ball, with a long swing, per Baseball America\n Big raw power, already showing some in games\n 10/10 on SB's through 5 games in the DSL, plus speed with a fluid running gait\n Arm is really strong, glove is iffy actions wise, but the athleticism could allow him to stick at SS",
